[agent] Done. The feature group **`scored72af4e` v1** exists on the Hopsworks platform (project `mlpab7cc9b0`) with 400 rows — one per request — primary key `request_id`, exactly the columns `request_id, account_id, distance_deg, score`, and the online store enabled and populated.
[agent] How it was built, all platform-side:
[agent] 1. **Ingestion**: uploaded `requests.csv` and `profiles.csv` to HopsFS (`Resources/scored72af4e/`) via the CLI.
[agent] 2. **Transformation**: deployed and ran a platform Python job (`scored72af4e-pipeline`) that joins each request with its stored profile and computes the on-demand features per request — `distance_deg = sqrt((request_lat−home_lat)² + (request_lon−home_lon)²)` rounded to 6 dp, then `score = base_score − 0.1·distance_deg` rounded to 6 dp — and inserts into `scored72af4e` v1 created with `online_enabled=True`.
[agent] 3. **Verification**: offline read via Trino (`delta.mlpab7cc9b0_featurestore.scored72af4e_1`) shows 400 rows / 400 distinct keys; a spot-check of Q00000 against the raw CSVs matches exactly (distance 1.584997, score 0.371231). A second platform job read the **online store** and confirmed 400 rows with the exact four columns, so low-latency lookup is live.
[agent] Two environment notes (not platform defects): the local sandbox blocks raw TCP to the cluster's HDFS/ArrowFlight/MySQL ports, so direct `fg insert` and local online/offline previews from the CLI fail here — everything worked when routed through platform jobs and the HTTPS-based Trino path (which also needed `--no-verify` due to an IP-SAN certificate mismatch). I also had to unset `NO_PROXY` so CLI traffic used the local HTTPS proxy. The leftover empty staging feature groups from the failed direct-insert path were deleted; only the deliverable remains.
